  "_comment": "Synonyms / everyday-language aliases for ISCED-F 2013 detailed codes. Concatenated into the per-code embedding doc so that resume-idiom queries (e.g. 'Computer Science', 'Culinary Arts') align with the bureaucratic ISCED label. Two entry shapes are supported per code: (1) a list of aliases — `\"0511\": [\"biology\", ...]` — uses the canonical detailed_name from the ISCED CSV as the doc's primary label; (2) a dict with `label` + `aliases` — `\"0111\": {\"label\": \"...\", \"aliases\": [...]}` — overrides the canonical name in the doc when its surface form leaks into unrelated queries (e.g. 'Education science' → magnetizes anything ending in '...science'). The canonical name is still used in CSV output and previews. Codes without an entry fall back to bare canonical + hierarchy.",

